{{define "content"}}<article class="security-page">
<h1>Security</h1>

<p>If you have found a security issue in {{.Base.SiteName}}, we want to hear
about it. Report it privately using one of the channels below — please do not
open a public issue or post details anywhere until we have had a chance to
fix it.</p>

<h2>How to report</h2>
<ol class="security-contacts">
{{if .ReportURL}}<li><strong>Private vulnerability report (preferred):</strong>
<a href="{{.ReportURL}}" rel="noopener">{{.ReportURL}}</a></li>{{end}}
{{if .ContactFormURL}}<li><strong>Security report form:</strong>
<a href="{{.ContactFormURL}}">report a vulnerability on this site</a></li>{{end}}
{{if .ContactEmail}}<li><strong>Email:</strong>
<a href="mailto:{{.ContactEmail}}">{{.ContactEmail}}</a></li>{{end}}
</ol>

<h2>What to include</h2>
<p>A clear summary, the exact URL or endpoint affected, the steps needed to
reproduce it, and what an attacker could achieve. If you have a suggested
fix, include it — it makes crediting you easier.</p>

{{if .HasPGPKey}}
<h2>Encryption</h2>
<p>Sensitive reports can be encrypted to our public key:
<a href="{{.PGPKeyURL}}">{{.PGPKeyURL}}</a>{{if .Keyservers}}, also published
to {{range $i, $k := .Keyservers}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}<a href="{{$k}}" rel="noopener">{{$k}}</a>{{end}}{{end}}.</p>
{{end}}

<h2>Policy</h2>
<p>Read our <a href="{{.PolicyURL}}">coordinated disclosure policy</a> before
testing, and see the researchers we have
<a href="{{.ThanksURL}}">credited</a>.</p>

<h2>Machine-readable</h2>
<p>This page mirrors <a href="{{.SecurityTxtURL}}">{{.SecurityTxtURL}}</a>
(RFC 9116). That file expires {{.Expires}}.</p>
</article>
{{end}}
